# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
**/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
**/coverage

# next.js
**/.next/
**/out/

# electron-builder installer output (.dmg / .exe / .AppImage) — never commit binaries
**/release/

# production
**/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# .claude — commit the team toolkit (agents/skills/settings.json); rules + workflows moved to method/,
# ignore personal + machine-local state
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# personal per-project preferences (Babich CLAUDE.local.md) — never committed
CLAUDE.local.md

# machine-local index caches from optional dev tooling — never committed
.codegraph/

# Internal dev framework (method/) + sprint lab (work/) now live IN the monorepo,
# TRACKED — but delivery-EXCLUDED (see `.gitattributes` export-ignore + the delivery
# canary, scripts/delivery-canary.mjs). `work/` must never reach a user; that holds
# ONLY because delivery is by allowlist (CLI copy / `git archive`), never a repo
# clone/hand-off. Their throwaway + machine-local state stays ignored:
work/scratch/
**/settings.local.json
.gstack/
**/_gstack
.context/

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Sanity typegen intermediate — regenerated by `pnpm sanity:typegen`.
# The generated types (src/sanity/sanity.types.ts) ARE committed; schema.json is not.
/code/projects/web/schema.json


# VitePress build output (docs site)
**/.vitepress/dist/
**/.vitepress/cache/
# generated: area changelogs copied into the docs site at build (sources under code/**/CHANGELOG.md)
docs/apps/web/changelog.md
docs/packages/changelog.md
docs/modules/changelog.md

# turbo cache
.turbo/
**/.turbo/

# Cloudflare (OpenNext) — build output, local wrangler state, local secrets
**/.open-next/
**/.wrangler/
**/.dev.vars
!**/.dev.vars.example

# Local backups — Sanity dataset dumps, D1 dumps, subscriber CSVs (may hold PII).
# Remote copies live in the R2 backups bucket, not git.
**/backups/
**/content-backups/

# storybook static build
**/storybook-static/
